          "rules": [
            { "id": "deepinit/IF-1", "name": "BusinessRuleViolation", "shortDescription": { "text": "Business-rule violation / inconsistent enforcement" } },
            { "id": "deepinit/IF-3a", "name": "SilentCrossComponentCoupling", "shortDescription": { "text": "A resource/contract shared across components with no explicit interface" } },
            { "id": "deepinit/IF-4", "name": "IntentDecisionContradiction", "shortDescription": { "text": "Code contradicts a documented decision/convention, or a name/route lies" } },
            { "id": "deepinit/IF-7", "name": "ErrorPathContradiction", "shortDescription": { "text": "Error/exception path swallows or contradicts intended behaviour" } },
            { "id": "deepinit/IF-9", "name": "RepoHygiene", "shortDescription": { "text": "Repository-hygiene defect (ignore rules, tracked-file gaps, build reproducibility)" } }
          ]
        }
      },
      "properties": {
        "runId": "deepinit-2026-08-17",
        "runKind": "incremental-update",
        "basedOnRun": "deepinit-2026-06-30",
        "sourceThroughCommit": "339a89c",
        "lifecycle": {
          "open": ["ISS-007", "ISS-011"],
          "accepted": ["ISS-003", "ISS-004"],
          "resolved": ["ISS-001", "ISS-002", "ISS-005", "ISS-006", "ISS-009", "ISS-010"],
          "regressed": [],
          "new": ["ISS-011"],
          "note": "All five components were dirty this run, so issue detection ran at full horizontal scope. ISS-010 moved to resolved (cfb8e36 added a source-only .gitignore re-include and tracked the 12 db/ files; re-verified via `git check-ignore -v` returning no match and both files appearing in `git ls-files`) and is dropped from active results. ISS-011 is NEW. ISS-007 re-verified persisting even though `common` was otherwise modified. ISS-003/ISS-004 remain accepted-by-design (suppressed); ISS-004's accepted-divergence list gained a sixth, behavioral member — Android at-most-once SMS dedup vs .NET Success-only."
        },
        "verification": [
          "node tools/parity-lint.mjs -> exit 0 across 5 value-sets",
          "git check-ignore -v on the former ISS-010 paths -> no match",
          "56 app.Map* vs 51 .RequireAuthorization in Program.cs -> difference == the 5 intentionally-public endpoints",
          "component content_hash method reproduced all five stored 2026-06-30 values at 46951bf before recomputation at HEAD"
        ]
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "deepinit/IF-1", "level": "warning", "baselineState": "unchanged",
          "message": { "text": "Hardcoded symmetric encryption-key constant: MagavConstants.PasswordKey is a source literal used by EncryptedConnectionStringsProvider.cs:46 to decrypt the DB connection string - anyone with the source can decrypt, defeating the at-rest encryption. PERSISTING: the related committed-appsettings-credentials half was resolved in 2989b01 (secrets externalized to env/user-secrets + a fail-loud JWT startup guard, ADR-017), but this constant and its use are unchanged - re-verified 2026-08-17 even though MagavConstants.cs was otherwise modified this run. Remediation: supply the key from an environment variable or secret store, and consider modernizing the cipher/KDF (legacy Rijndael + default Rfc2898DeriveBytes iterations). Secret VALUE is never reproduced (R5)." },
          "locations": [ { "physicalLocation": { "artifactLocation": { "uri": "web/server/Magav.Common/MagavConstants.cs" }, "region": { "startLine": 7 } } } ],
          "partialFingerprints": { "deepinitMatchKey": "IF-1:web/server/Magav.Common/MagavConstants.cs:PasswordKey#hardcoded" },
          "properties": { "iss": "ISS-007", "severity": "Medium", "criticality": "Core", "certainty": "HIGH", "lifecycle": "persisting", "firstSeenRun": "deepinit-2026-06-18" }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "deepinit/IF-1", "level": "warning", "baselineState": "new",
          "message": { "text": "The message-template in-use guard does not cover the administrative template ROLES. MessageTemplateRepository.IsInUseAsync (and its Android twin MessageTemplateDao.getUsageCount) count only SchedulerConfig.MessageTemplateId references, but the administrative assignment/today templates are referenced by id stored as AppSettings VALUES (admin_assignment_template_id / admin_today_template_id). An Admin can therefore delete an in-use administrative template. It does not self-heal: the startup migration re-creates the template by name (getting a NEW auto-increment id) while the AppSettings key is seeded INSERT OR IGNORE / once-only, so the key keeps pointing at the deleted id. Effect is fail-safe but silent - administrative SMS sends return 'template not configured' until an Admin re-picks the template. The advance template is unaffected (referenced by the AdminAdvance SchedulerConfig row, which the guard does cover). Present identically on both backends. Fix: extend the in-use check to also count AppSettings rows whose Key is an admin template-role key and whose Value equals the template id - on both backends; or make the AppSettings seed repair a key whose template no longer exists." },
          "locations": [
            { "physicalLocation": { "artifactLocation": { "uri": "web/server/Magav.Server/Database/Repositories/MessageTemplateRepository.cs" }, "region": { "startLine": 13, "endLine": 18 } } },
            { "physicalLocation": { "artifactLocation": { "uri": "android/app/src/main/java/com/magav/app/db/dao/MessageTemplateDao.kt" }, "region": { "startLine": 36, "endLine": 37 } } }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": { "deepinitMatchKey": "IF-1:web/server/Magav.Server/Database/Repositories/MessageTemplateRepository.cs:IsInUseAsync#appsettings-refs-uncovered" },
          "properties": { "iss": "ISS-011", "severity": "Medium", "criticality": "Supporting", "certainty": "HIGH", "lifecycle": "new", "firstSeenRun": "deepinit-2026-08-17", "autoAccepted": false }
        }
      ],
      "suppressions_note": "ISS-003 and ISS-004 are accepted-by-design (ADR-016 / ADR-001+012+015 with the ADR-018 parity lint as mitigation) and are not emitted as active results. ISS-008 is a deterministic risk RANKING, not a defect, and is not emitted. ISS-010 is resolved and dropped. Candidates considered and NOT raised this run (stated for honesty): the non-transactional administrative create (identical on both backends, retry-idempotent), the unlinted AppSettingsKeys mirroring obligation (fragility, not a current defect), and the global Locations.Name uniqueness across both types (verified intentional)."
    }
  ]
}
